{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) has issued stitch task #5620 to implement `cmd/dircolors` for the go-unix-utils project. Specifically, the task requires implementing SRD109 requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, and R1.4 (shell output format), creating two files (`cmd/dircolors/main.go` and `cmd/dircolors/dircolors_test.go`), and ensuring all acceptance criteria pass. The task is part of an automated code generation pipeline where git is managed externally.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **dircolors utility**: Outputs shell commands to set the LS_COLORS environment variable for colorized `ls` output\n   - **Differential testing**: Go binary compared against GNU reference binary `gdircolors` (Homebrew) via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **Shell output formats**: Bourne shell (`LS_COLORS='<value>';\\nexport LS_COLORS`) vs C shell (`setenv LS_COLORS '<value>'`)\n   - **Shell auto-detection**: SHELL env var ending in \"csh\" → C shell format, otherwise Bourne\n   - **Flag precedence**: -b and -c are mutually exclusive, last one wins\n   - **GNU dircolors database format**: Comments (#), TERM entries, file type keywords (DIR, LINK, EXEC, etc.) mapped to two-letter LS_COLORS codes (di, ln, ex, etc.), and extension mappings (*.tar=01;31)\n   - **Built-in default database**: Must match `gdircolors --print-database` output\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at start of main\n   - **Keyword-to-code mapping**: DIR=di, LINK=ln, EXEC=ex, FIFO=pi, SOCK=so, BLK=bd, CHR=cd, ORPHAN=or, SETUID=su, SETGID=sg, STICKY=st, OTHER_WRITABLE=ow, STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE=tw, CAPABILITY=ca, MULTIHARDLINK=mh, NORMAL=no, FILE=fi, RESET=rs, MISSING=mi, LEFT=lc, RIGHT=rc, END=ec\n\n3. Files and Code S