{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AcecbpdhX94NfmwZxGSxfv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. They just discard stderr entirely in some tests. For my case, I can use a normalizer that strips the binary name prefix from stderr. But actually, the simpler approach is to just discard stderr for those error cases since I can't control what name the binary runs as.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully, I think the approach should be to create a normalizer that replaces both `gdircolors` and `dircolors` (and any full path) in the stderr output with a common name. Let me also check the `MakeBinaryNameNormalizer` or similar.\n\n\nLooking at the testutils code, I don't see a built-in binary name normalizer, so I need to check how other tests handle error messages when the binary name varies.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":64976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":269},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"887394ca-6926-4248-87fe-87134d407a7a","uuid":"e948beb2-0e88-4476-8113-788f3b74abba"}
